NAME
       lastlog - show when each user last logged in

SYNOPSIS
       lastlog

DESCRIPTION
       lastlog prints one line per account in /etc/passwd: the name, the
       terminal and host of the last login, and its time, or "**Never logged
       in**". It reads /var/log/lastlog. Service accounts normally never log
       in; a service account with a login time is worth a closer look.

EXAMPLES
           lastlog | grep -v Never

FILES
       /var/log/lastlog

SEE ALSO
       last(1), login(1)
